Z||000002||fierosound||08-14-2000||11:43 PM||||I saw a Fiero at the dragstrip last time I was there.  I went down to the pits and chatted with him.  <P>He had a 3.4L pushrod engine with:<P>high comp pistons<BR>sprint exhaust manifolds<BR>high-perf cam (not sure what)<BR>4 BBL holley ON TOP of plenum<BR>HUGE air-scoop on top of hood<BR>some type of low restriction exhaust<BR>and NOS (not sure how much)<BR>also an AUTOMATIC transmission<P>The best time he ran was 13.92 @ 97mph with nitrous.<P>PS- we're at 3500 ft elevation here...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/alsfiero.jpg">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 08-15-2000).]||||reg||10
